First, I disagree with your closing assessment. You said there's really nothing exciting learned here. I think you learned quite a bit, actually.
The great Companions pacifist experiment.
You discovered that your original plan — let Arniel, Serana and Little Blue handle everything — runs into a very particular problem: the Companions' initiation test expects you to demonstrate some fighting ability.
And the followers made an absolute dog's breakfast of the first attempt. 😂
Arniel started blasting, Blue got involved, Serana got involved, and suddenly the whole yard became a free-for-all. Vilkas couldn't properly evaluate you because everyone was fighting everyone.
But you worked out the important part: followers need to be dismissed or told to wait elsewhere before the test begins. Otherwise their combat AI interferes with the scripted encounter.
Then you discovered that you could pass the test by blocking and eventually landing a hit. You didn't have to become a warrior. You just had to demonstrate that you could defend yourself and give Vilkas something to evaluate.
And that brings me to something I rather like about your approach.
